      summary: 'Before this, every new NLP task needed thousands of labeled examples and a round of fine-tuning. The OpenAI team trained GPT-3, a 175-billion-parameter autoregressive model on 300 billion tokens of filtered web text, and tested it on over two dozen tasks using only in-context examples. In the few-shot setting (10 to 100 examples in the prompt, zero gradient updates), GPT-3 hit 85.0 F1 on CoQA and 71.2% on TriviaQA, matching or beating fine-tuned state-of-the-art models. It also generated news articles that human evaluators had difficulty distinguishing from real ones. The team trained 8 model sizes from 125M to 175B parameters and showed that in-context learning ability grows smoothly with scale.',
