      inYourTools: 'When you paste a few examples into a chat and the model copies the pattern, that is the few-shot, in-context learning this paper measured. It works with any model you run in Ollama, LM Studio or llama.cpp; bigger models are usually better at it, just as the paper found.',
      readThis: [
        'Figure 1.1: The diagram that explains in-context learning as a two-loop process: broad skills from pre-training, then rapid task adaptation at inference time.',
        'Figure 1.3: The aggregate bar chart across 42 benchmarks showing that few-shot performance rises much faster with model size than zero-shot does.',
        'Table 3.3: The closed-book QA results where GPT-3\'s few-shot TriviaQA score of 71.2% beats the fine-tuned open-domain SOTA of 68.0%.',
      ],
      skipThis: 'Section 4 (data contamination analysis) and Section 6 (broader societal impacts, bias, and energy usage) are long policy discussions that a hobbyist can safely skim.',
      terms: [
        ('few-shot learning', 'Giving a model a handful of examples in the prompt so it figures out the task.'),
