    Paper(
      sourceId: 'SRC-QLORA',
      short: 'QLoRA',
      year: '2023',
      authors: 'Tim Dettmers et al., University of Washington',
      oneIdea: 'Freeze the base model at 4-bit and train only tiny adapter weights. This slashes training memory so a 65B model fits on one 48 GB GPU without losing accuracy.',
      summary: 'Finetuning a 65B-parameter model in full 16-bit precision needs more than 780 GB of GPU memory, far beyond what a single card can hold. QLoRA keeps the base model frozen at 4-bit using a new data type called NormalFloat, and trains only small LoRA adapter weights. Three extra tricks keep memory low: Double Quantization compresses the quantization constants themselves, and Paged Optimizers offload optimizer states to CPU RAM when the GPU runs out of space. The result is a 65B model finetuned on a single 48 GB GPU in 24 hours, reaching 99.3% of ChatGPT\'s score on the Vicuna chatbot benchmark. The authors trained over 1,000 models this way and found that a small, high-quality dataset (9k samples) beats a much larger one (450k samples) for chatbot performance.',
      whyItMattered: 'Before QLoRA, adapting the largest open models to your own data required multi-GPU servers. Now a single consumer or professional GPU is enough, which means hobbyists and small teams can personalize large models at home. It became the default method for fine-tuning open-weight models on a budget.',
      inYourTools: 'QLoRA is how most hobbyists fine-tune: libraries such as Hugging Face PEFT with bitsandbytes, Unsloth and Axolotl let you train LoRA adapters on a 4-bit base model on a single consumer GPU. The NF4 data type from this paper is the bitsandbytes 4-bit format; it is not the same thing as llama.cpp\'s GGUF quants.',
      readThis: [
        'Figure 1: Side-by-side memory comparison of full finetuning, LoRA, and QLoRA, showing how quantization and paged optimizers close the gap.',
        'Section 3: The three core innovations — 4-bit NormalFloat, Double Quantization, and Paged Optimizers — explained step by step.',
        'Table 6: Vicuna benchmark scores for every model and dataset combination, showing Guanaco 65B at 99.3% of ChatGPT.',
