      summary: 'Transformers are strong at language but slow on long sequences because their cost grows quadratically with context length. Earlier fast alternatives called state space models were too rigid: they used the same fixed rules for every token and could not tell important content from noise. The authors made the model\'s internal parameters depend on the input, so it can selectively focus on relevant tokens and ignore the rest. They also designed a hardware-aware algorithm that keeps this selective computation fast on modern GPUs. The result is a model with no attention and no separate MLP blocks that runs 5x faster than Transformers and matches a Transformer twice its size in quality.',
