      summary: 'Open-source models were falling behind closed-source ones, and training large models was prohibitively expensive. DeepSeek built a Mixture-of-Experts model with 671B total parameters but only 37B active per token, using Multi-head Latent Attention for efficient inference and a new auxiliary-loss-free load balancing trick to keep all experts busy without hurting quality. They also added a multi-token prediction training objective that densifies learning signals. Trained on 14.8 trillion tokens on 2048 H800 GPUs, the model scored 90.2 on MATH-500 and 75.9 on MMLU-Pro, matching GPT-4o and Claude-3.5-Sonnet on several benchmarks. The entire training run cost 2.788M GPU hours (\$5.576M) with no loss spikes or rollbacks.',
